libxmp-lite 4.7.2, embedded PS2 build
=====================================

Source:
  https://github.com/libxmp/libxmp/releases/tag/libxmp-4.7.2

Imported archive:
  libxmp-lite-4.7.2.tar.gz
  SHA-256: bace7f53248a2cd5adcf77f9402a8858fc0fec05f4e6d6436e3d2a28d68f640e

Matching upstream tag commit:
  a13276d27feabcf9ee4f982913f718ee05a65cb7

The public header and libxmp-lite source are vendored for a deterministic
cross-build. SNESticle Revive compiles the embedded/core configuration with
LIBXMP_CORE_PLAYER from its main Makefile. The menu scanner currently exposes
only MOD and XM files even though the library also contains S3M and IT loaders.

The PS2 integration sets XMP_PLAYER_DEFPAN to 50 before loading a module. This
keeps classic hard-panned MOD channels audible on displays or receivers whose
mono/downmix path would otherwise make instruments appear to disappear.

See LICENSE for the MIT license.
